# Convex Docker pod pairing (agents)

## Why pairing keeps coming back

Pairing is **not a one-time install step**. It binds:

1. **Browser origin** (`http://127.0.0.1:<caddyPort>`) — localStorage / session for the web UI
2. **Server auth session** — stored in the pod's **Postgres + `t3code_home` Docker volumes**

Re-pairing is **expected** when any of these happen:

| Cause | What agents did | Fix |
|-------|-----------------|-----|
| **Volume wipe** | `destroy`, `docker volume rm`, or fresh bootstrap during tests | Run `bootstrap-pairing-url` and open the Caddy pairing link once |
| **Wrong origin** | Opened raw Vite (`:6657` / `:8207`) instead of Caddy (`:8080` / `:8081`) | Always use **Caddy URL** from manifest `caddyUrl` for browse + pair |
| **New Convex deployment** | New `postgres_data` after cold start | Same as volume wipe — new pairing token |
| **noVNC only** | Electron runs in VNC but host browser never paired at Caddy | Pair in **host browser** at Caddy URL, not only inside VNC |

**Do not** treat repeated pairing as a bug unless volumes are preserved **and** the user always uses the same Caddy origin.

## Agent workflow (mandatory)

After `pod:up`, `start-pod`, or any pod restart that wiped volumes:

```bash
./.agents/scripts/t3-convex-docker.sh bootstrap-pairing-url t3code-staging
# or: pnpm run pod:pair
```

Open the printed `pairing_url` in the **host** browser (Caddy origin). `pod:open` now opens this automatically when the stack is ready.

## Preserve pairing (avoid unnecessary resets)

- Prefer `./.agents/scripts/t3-convex-docker.sh down <slug>` — **does not** remove volumes.
- **Never** `destroy` or `docker volume rm` on `t3code_home` / `postgres_data` unless the user explicitly wants a clean slate.
- When testing pod bases or redeploying, warn the user that pairing will be required again.

## Stable URLs per slug (LOCAL_ONLY)

| Slug | Caddy (pair here) | Raw Vite (do not pair here) |
|------|-------------------|-----------------------------|
| `t3code-staging` | `http://127.0.0.1:8080` | `http://127.0.0.1:6657` |
| `t3code-main` | `http://127.0.0.1:8081` | `http://127.0.0.1:8207` |

Electron in noVNC: http://127.0.0.1:8080/vnc/vnc.html (view only — pairing still happens at Caddy app URL).

## Pod CLIs (Codex + Tailscale)

Both are **baked into `Dockerfile.t3-pod`** and verified on boot by `install-pod-cli-tools.sh`.

| CLI | Out of the gate | One-time user setup |
|-----|-----------------|---------------------|
| **Codex** | On PATH in every pod | OAuth: `docker exec … codex login --device-auth` |
| **Tailscale** | CLI on PATH in every pod | Save `tskey-auth-…` to `~/.local/share/t3code-local/convex-docker/ts-authkey`, then `provision` + `up` |

Without `ts-authkey`, pods run LOCAL_ONLY — Tailscale CLI is still present but no sidecar daemon.

See `infra/convex-docker/README.md` and `.context/docs.md` (Agent-maintained notes → Pod pairing).
